llama-server (b11549): a completion prompt with images on a non-causal context goes whole into one batch.

A prompt-bidirectional (Instant) model must read the text and the image embeddings of a prompt together in one
micro-batch. The server does that (add_prompt_mixed) only for embedding tasks; a completion with images was decoded as
text before the image, the image, and the text after it (three micro-batches), which cuts the bidirectional attention.
The patch makes such a prompt non-splittable: it is evaluated whole in one batch, and a prompt longer than -ub is
refused (never cut). /props reports mtmd_prompt_whole_when_non_causal so that clients can tell. Causal contexts and
prompts without images are unchanged. Apply with: patch -p1 < 0003-... (applies to stock b11549 and on top of 0001).

diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -446,6 +446,11 @@
 
     bool can_split() const {
         GGML_ASSERT(task);
+        // a prompt with images on a non-causal context is read whole: its text tokens and its image embeddings go into
+        // one batch (add_prompt_mixed), so that every prompt token attends to every other (prompt-bidirectional models)
+        if (task->tokens.has_mtmd && !llama_get_causal_attn(ctx_tgt)) {
+            return false;
+        }
         // MTP supports splitting - uses task->need_embd() not need_embd()
         if (!task->need_embd()) {
             return true;
@@ -5130,6 +5135,7 @@
             {"audio",  meta.has_inp_audio},
         } },
         { "media_marker",                get_media_marker() },
+        { "mtmd_prompt_whole_when_non_causal", true },
         { "endpoint_slots",              params.endpoint_slots },
         { "endpoint_props",              params.endpoint_props },
         { "endpoint_metrics",            params.endpoint_metrics },
